Ideas:
- multiplayer game
    - Players securely login
    - Customize their players name, face, body, etc.
    - start with zero tools
    - can train animals as pets
    - has a login screen
    - starts off in a random location within the "inside" of the world map

- World Map
    - procedurally generated map.
        - Minecraft generation is appealing given its rich diversity of land features
            - such as really high mountains, caves, and under water diversity
        - Unlike minecraft, there shouldn't be floating islands in the "inside" map as those don't exist.
            - perhaps on other planets this mechanic would allowed.
    - Once generated, the map doesn't change unless we introduce mechanics to allow change.
    - Players can build houses and other things on land and water.
    - PLayers need to mark their territory so that it's not "nerfed" by other players.
    - Need to store generated chunks.
    - Tornadoes, floods, volcanic runoff, extreme wet and dry seasons can change the map
    - "fog of war" type maps, where everything is black or fogged out until explored.
    - Some water is bluer than others.  This is important for quests related for my "wifey".
        - she wants to find the bluest water in the map.  Talking like Antigua blue!
- "flat earth" theme
   - Earth is not really "flat", that's just stupid.  It's much much bigger than we're taught.
   - The map we're taught and know of within the overall "flat earth" game map is considered "inside".
- players start on an island, could be U.S. or some land mass on the "inside"
- "Inside"
   - Relatively safe, minimal combat if any.
   - More of exploring the world that we know today.
   - Players can build and live peacefully, run businesses, shops, build houses, farms, have farm animals, etc.
   - Map Landscape varies, just like all of the earth's wonderful, distinct, and in some places outlandish features.
   - Some mountains look like enormous tree trunks "for a reason".
   - Some mountains and other land masses look like large human like creatures fossilized "for a reason".
   - We don't yet know what happened to them or how those came to be.
   - As players work through quests and explore outside the first ring, some parts of game play pull them back in.
      - Need to have a hook, storyline, perhaps unlocked resources or something to pull players back "inside".
      - Perhaps with quests or challenges or maybe unlocked resources after venturing and exploring the outer ring(s).
   - NPC villages may or may not have special resources available
- "First Ring"
   - Creates a boundary of sorts around the "Inside".
   - Earth maps that were taught show Antartica as a sourthern land mass
   - Flat Earth says antartica is actually an ice wall, surrounds the "inside"
   - All powerful governments protect antartica, seemingly because of the extreme frigid temps
   - Holds special blue ice
   - Unknown hidden channel or channels can be found and navigated
   - The ring is a land mass that's spans 100 miles to the other side
   - Within the ring, it's frigid, snow and ice storms, very hard to survive without proper gear and supplies
   - Governments of global powers has presence here, masked as "research" initiatives
   - Civilian exploration hasn't been opening denied, however environment conditions make it virtually impossible to travel
   - There are also hard to see and find government facilities within the ice wall with huge doors that lead into tunnels.
   - Within the tunnels is miles of other tunnels within the ring.
   - Highest level clearance is needed to navigate through and reach the outside of the inner ring.
- Beyond the first ring, there are different zones or realms
    - land masses can be huge, some small, some an archipelago
    - each zone or realm has a different theme
    - Some zone or realm themes:
        - Extremely large distances to travel over water to reach a zone or realm
            - just impractical for ships
             - unless you know where islands along the way are located and can stay to replenish supplies
        - greek mythology
            - maybe the kraken would be a boss
            - or zeus's father would be a boss
            - zeus and his family would be there
            - of course medusa.
            - very hard to reach, for obvious reasons
            - lush, green, easy to grow things
        - Desert.
            - Extremely dry.  Extreme hot during day. Extreme cold at night.
            - liveable but difficult, obviously hard to get water and food.
            - learn to live off scorpions, snakes, and discover rare water sources.
        - Dinosaurs.
            - Volcanoes, hot, humid, lots of vegetation
            - Different kinds of dinosaurs: walking, flying, swimming, florescent, mythical looking beasts.
        - Middle Earth.
            - Lord of the rings theme. probably have to be careful here with copyright.
            - Lots of famouns places include
                - Shire
                - deep in the sea is Numenor
                - Moria
                - Rivendelle
                - woodland elf region
                - Beorn's place
                - Tom Bombadil's place
                - Maybe the land where elves originated is the in 2nd ring.
        - Wheel of Time
            - Supports humans and dark side creatures Channeling powers or magic.
            - Thinking to include all the different races, beasts, and characters, and regions.
- Haven't decided how many rings to have in the full world map.
- Each zone or realm will have unique properties as describe.
    - Do we have NPCs running in those areas or allow players to somehow travel back in time when they existed
    - How do we explain their demise
    - If we allow travel back, then we need full storylines, NCPs, and quests to relive that region.
    - Each zone or realm somehow needs tie of some sorts into an overall theme for the game.
    - Haven't decided if powers and special abilities from each zone would be possible in other zones
        - Might be limited to objects inbued with powers
        - A player starting as a channeler from Camelyn or White Tower could explore other realms and zones
            - Powers would likely be limited or even cut off "somehow" to keep a balance in the game.
- There needs to be a reason why beasts and people from "outside" hasn't reached "inside".
- Do we consider each Realm or Zone as the main epicenter of the world during a give "age"?
    - Then as each age ended, the epicenter shifted to another realm where that region became the epicenter for a time.
    - Then at the end of that age, the land became abandoned.
    - Does the "inside" regoin become the refuge of people as a last bastion of hope for human civilization to continue?
- If all Realms and Zones actively exist, the each needs a tech tree that can sufficiently defend against other realm powers
    - For example - "Inside" abilities would be nuclear, chemical, and maybe even biological warfare weapons and tech.

- One storyline concept is these other areas are mainly abandoned
    - Players learn that massive wars occurred in the second outer ring realms.
    - Through exploration and quests you can pick up special abilities, recipes, tech, powers to help achieve a greater goal.

- You learn that the earth is actually 100x bigger and has suffered the fate of many great civilizations
    - where the people groups get too comfortable, too "liberal"
    - fall into the trap of sin that erodes away tradition, Belief in Jesus, and ultimately fall apart.

- The target goal for the "inside" region is to build a tech tree that ulimately creates vessels, ships, etc.

- Toying with the idea to incorporate a Battlestar Galactica theme
    - Players are explore "inside" and "outside" the rings but come to the realization that the planet is dying.
    - Ultimate goal is to build a tech tree to learn rocketry, physics, chemicals, aviation, space, and space travel
    - Build a ship that can leave our orbit, find and reach another solar system, and recolonize there.
    - Realize that our civilization has been there before, sent during a previous age.
    - Discover that we've built 'battlestars' great military vessels which can defend againsts robots drive by AI
    - AI intelligence has determined that humans are too destructive, doesn't look out for its good, and needs to be eliminated
    - This concept might be best discovered outside the 2nd or 3rd ring of the world map
        - Otherwise it doesn't fit well with the King/Queen era starting point
    - Important deviation from the tv series is that instead of searching for Earth, we're not searching for another planet to settle

- Another concept - maybe some realms mentioned above are actually found on other planets.
    - Might explain why realms haven't mixed.
    - Might increase space exploration.
    - Not sure how special powers and tech can be limited to the native worlds or restricted or even should be.
    - Even with this concept, there would be realms of some sort outside of the "inside" ring
    - there would be reasons why players would need to explore there for special resources
    - technologies which have been long lost due to wars and conflicts that help you reach the next level.

- There's some metal, mineral, or resource "inside" that ties all other realms together.
    - We're on the same planet after all.
    - Perhaps some resource types unlock after certain quests to the outside.
    - These give players ability to craft or build tech which can't be done for some reason in the outer rings and realms.

- Thinking there needs to be NPCs and quests to help players explore the world and discover the other worlds.
    - All NPCs needs a backstory, who are they, where they came from, what they do
    - Some NPCs are 'main' characters, other NPCs are supporting characters of the main one
    - Even some NPCs exist to support supporting NPCs to the main character NPCs.

- Players have various attributes:
    - Faith - one of the important player attributes
        - Increases with belief in God, Jesus, Holy Spirit.
        - Increases a players 'will' to live through hard challenges and environments which are difficult to survive.
    - Intelligence - determines how quickly players can pick up and understand tech
    - other basic attributes will be there, like strength, health, etc.
    - For the beach lovers, like my wifey, we need an attributes
        - UV protection - for skin burn which requires them to wear sunscreen
        - Replenishment - fruity drinks, some with little umbrellas

    - Players clothes, armor, accessories, vehicles, vehicle components, etc determines how well they can survive extreme environments and battle enemies.
    - Player weapons determine how well they inflict damage.

- Another concept - incorporate educational aspects to the game that make it fun for kids to learn different topics such as:
    - money literacy - how to invest money into the market early
    - math, colors, names of things for kids
    - electricity - understand principles of electricity, how to wire different types of systems up including solar power
    - chemistry - understanding principles of inorganic chemistry
        - Learn reactions.
        - Important for certain quests in the game.
        - Critical path for developing resources and technology for space travel
    - physics, biology and others.









